/-!
# `Work.ThmF.ChV3.Prove.A_LV_aux` — setup for §3 step (15d) (`A_LV_facts`)

Peterfalvi II, Ch. V §3, step (15d) (the last leaf of the §3 second half) states that
`A = Z₁ P Σ` is elementary abelian of order `27`, that `L V` has order `27 |W|` with `A`
its subgroup of elements of order dividing `3`, and that `Z₁ Σ` is central in `L V`.

This module collects the structural facts about the objects
`Z₁ = ⟨st⟩`, `P`, `Σ = C_W(P)`, `L = X₅ ∩ C_G(st)`, `V = C_D(t)`, `W = C_V(K)`
that are needed, all of them consequences of the standing context `CtxF`, the chain
`Chain15`, and the case-(10-2) data.  The main ingredients:

* `P ≤ C_G(st)` and hence `[Z₁, P] = 1`;
* `P` normalises `L`, `W` and (`hence`) `L ⊔ W`;
* the action of the `3`-group `P` on `L/Z₁` and on `W/Σ`, both of order dividing `3`,
  is trivial because `Aut(C₃) ≅ C₂`; this gives `[L,P] ≤ Z₁` and `[W,P] ≤ Σ`;
* `Σ = Ω₁(W)` and `Z₁ = Ω₁(L)`;
* `L ⊓ V = 1`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

